===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The act of [[consult]]ing together [[formally]]; [[serious]] [[conversation]] or [[discussion]]; [[interchange]] of [[view]]s.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Julius Caesar|IV|ii|passage=Nor with such free and friendly '''conference''' / As he hath used of old.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Sketches of Life and Character|passage=Mr. Wiley, a lawyer of some ability, was sitting in his office one day, when an elderly gentleman came in and asked to have a few words of '''conference''' with him.|year=1850|author=T. S. Arthur|page=129|authorlink=Timothy Shay Arthur|pageurl=https://www.google.com/books/edition/Sketches_of_Life_and_Character/mB0tAAAAYAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&pg=PA129|chapter=Seed Time and Harvest|oclc=1087079145|publisher=J. W. Bradley|location=Philadelphia|url=https://www.google.com/books/edition/Sketches_of_Life_and_Character/mB0tAAAAYAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=0}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} The act of [[compare|comparing]] two or more things together; [[comparison]].
#* {{RQ:Hooker Laws
|passage=helps and furtherances which {{...}} the mutual '''conference''' of all men's collections and observations may afford}}
# {{lb|en|politics}} A [[multilateral]] [[diplomatic]] [[negotiation]].
# {{lb|en|academia}} A formal [[event]] where scientists or other [[scholar]]s present their research results in [[speech]]es, [[workshop]]s, [[poster]]s or by other means.
# {{lb|en|business}} An event organized by a for-profit or [[non-profit]] organization to discuss a pressing issue, such as a new product, market trend or government regulation, with a range of speakers.
# {{lb|en|sports}} A group of [[sports]] [[team]]s that play each other on a regular basis.
# {{lb|en|Philippines|sports}} A [[constituent]] [[tournament]] of a sports league in a given season.
# {{lb|en|Methodist Church}} A stated meeting of [[preacher]]s and others, [[invest]]ed with [[authority]] to take [[cognizance]] of [[ecclesiastical]] matters.
# {{lb|en|Christianity}} A [[voluntary]] [[association]] of [[Congregational church]]es of a [[district]]; the district in which such churches are.
# {{lb|en|chiefly|Christianity}} A [[talk]] or [[lecture]], {{lb|en|Catholicism}} especially when given as part of a [[retreat]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1996|author=Kenneth R. Guindon|title=The King's Highway|publisher=Ignatius Press|isbn=9780898705812|page=114
|text=“{{...}}But I do know of a man who is an expert on the topic. In fact, he gave a '''conference''' here in our church not very long ago.{{...}}”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2000|author=Phil Kilroy|title=Madeleine Sophie Barat, 1779-1865: A Life|publisher=Paulist Press|isbn=9780809105267|page=109
|text=She gave a '''conference''' each evening during the retreat while Fr Dubas gave two talks during the day.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=Frederick Vaughan|title=Retreat from Manresa: A Jesuit Story|publisher=iUniverse|isbn=9781462009121|page=25
|text=Frank Underhill listened intensely as Father Master began his '''conference''' that first evening after prayers in chapel at 7:00 p.m. with an enthusiastic and entertaining account of his own first night in the Society{{...}}.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2019-07-01|title=A Vital Sketch of the Divine Revelation in the Books of Exodus, Leviticus, and Numbers concerning God's Economy with His Chosen and Redeemed People|journal=The Ministry of the Word|volume=23|number=07: Crystallization-Study of Numbers (2)|publisher=Living Stream Ministry
|text=When Brother Lee came to the United States, the first '''conference''' he gave was in 1962 on the all-inclusive Christ. All the attendees were new ones, yet he did not consider that the all-inclusive Christ was too high for them. No, he gave a '''conference''' on the all-inclusive Christ, including all these points from the books of Exodus, Leviticus, and Numbers.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2024|author=Charles Wright|title=The Way of the Heart: The Spiritual Experience of André Louf|publisher=Liturgical Press|isbn=9780879073374|page=268
|text=In July 2004 in Finland he gave a '''conference''' on the link between prayer and ecology, and in July 2006, speaking to some German deaconesses, he gave an an-yet-unpublished '''conference''' on a similar topic titled “Transfiguration as an Icon of the Consecrated Life.”}}

